5	Cowboys from Hell Preseason 2016	<h4>After capturing the 2015 FFBL American League pennant and a second straight bronze trophy, the Cowboys From Hell are poised to make another run for the Championship in 2016. For winning his division, manager Jeff Varnum was able to draft this year's American League, which he is hoping will help control his destiny. \r\n<br/>\r\nPlagued by off-the-field distractions from Chapman, Reyes, and Puig, the Cowboys will begin the season at a slight disadvantage as some of their starters will be suspended from major league play. A deep minor league system of major league ready talent should help alleviate this issue. \r\n<br/>\r\nIn the latest supplemental draft, Varnum targeted starters on the cusp of the major leagues; Nick Tropeano, Clayton Blackburn and Marco Gonzales. Said Varnum "if just one of these young hurlers can be relied upon for a few quality spot starts, then I'll consider this draft a success." It is noteworthy that his first selection came in the 3rd round of the draft. \r\n<br/>\r\nAlso acquired in the draft was J.J. Hoover, a quiet selection of a strong major league reliever who will begin the season in a closing role, which Varnum says will help deal with the suspension of Chapman. \r\n<br/>\r\nContrary to the off-the-field news of his players, this offseason was quiet for Varnum on the trade front, baring witness to Varnum making only a handful of transactions, all of which revolved around picks and prospects. He believes that this foretells of a confidence with the core of his team as it stands. \r\n<br/>\r\nAs has been the case for a few years now, the franchise's pitching was its calling card again in 2015. This season should be no different as the team's aces&mdash;Bumgarner, Sale, Fernandez and Hernandez&mdash;are ready to post quality starts at a rate most FFBL franchises only dream of. The team is looking forward to being bolstered by a full season from Jose Fernandez, FFBL's 2013 Rookie of the Year. \r\n<br/>\r\nThe offense will again be lead by Todd Frazier, Chris Davis, and Matt Carpenter. Disappointing seasons from Yasiel Puig and Jose Reyes held the team's offense back to a league average level last year. The Cowboys have a surplus of batters, and manager Jeff Varnum is hoping that the quantity of batters will make up for the difference in quality from the top tier teams, or perhaps for a couple of his players to outperform their expected play. A resurgence from Yasiel Puig would go a long way in bringing back the team's offensive impact. \r\n<br/>\r\nAfter about 30 games, the team should be back at full force as also expected back around that time is the exciting Devon Travis who showed brilliance last year before his season was cut short by injuries. Brilliance like that is precisely what the Cowboys from Hell need, particularly as the season wears on. The team is playoff caliber, and falling short of the championship round will be considered a disappointment. \r\n<br/>\r\nThis last paragraph is just fluff since I now no longer have control over my custom pages, so my means of making sure what I write here lines up well with the right column of ranks and projections. I even made the font size larger and added more line breaks, but the width of this column is too large to properly fit the short blurbs I used to write, and has way too much blank space around it. The old ones don't line up evenly anymore either. Maybe I should just ask Matt to reduce the line heights for that right column, because this is really going to bother me. I don't have anything else to say. Long live crappy old HTML editing in notepad.exe. There, that should just about wrap this mess up. Just another line more... or two. For fuck sake, just wrap to the next line and match the length of the right column. \r\n</h4>	Jesse Winker, of	Max Kepler, 1b/of	Jorge Alfaro, c	Chance Sisco, c	Marco Gonzales, sp	Derek Fisher, of	Rob Kaminsky, sp	Clayton Blackburn, sp	Zach Lee, sp	Jonathan Harris, sp	Andrew Susac	Chris Davis	Devon Travis	Todd Frazier	Wilmer Flores	Yasiel Puig	Colby Rasmus	Jesse Winker	Matt Carpenter	Mitch Moreland	Madison Bumgarner	Chris Sale	Jose Fernandez	Aroldis Chapman	Kenley Jansen	Huston Street	Felix Hernandez	Jose Quintana	C.J. Cron	Josh Harrison	Max Kepler	Jaime Garcia	Mike Leake	Marco Gonzales	Clayton Blackburn	2006	2007	2008	2009	2010	2011	2012	2013	2014	2015	Rich Hill, sp	Miguel Montero, c	Kosuke Fukudome, of	Madison Bumgarner, sp	Madison Bumgarner, sp	Aroldis Chapman, rp	Matt Moore, DL	Jose Fernandez, sp	Addison Russell, ss	Jesse Winker, of	The Bluth Company	Cowboys from Hell	Free Agent (Japan)	Cowboys from Hell	Cowboys from Hell	Cowboys from Hell	Scranton Yankees	Cowboys from Hell	Scranton Yankees	Cowboys from Hell	2007	2008	2009	2010	2011	2012	2013	2014	2015	2016	Livan Hernandez, sp	Kosuke Fukudome, of	Dayan Viciedo, of	Aroldis Chapman, rp	Chris Sale, sp	Leonys Martin, of	Addison Russell, 2b/ss	Hunter Harvey, sp	Monte Harrison, of²	Nick Tropeano, sp³	Retired	Playing in Japan	Free Agent	Cowboys from Hell	Cowboys from Hell	Free Agent	Scranton Yankees	Scranton Yankees	Cowboys from Hell	Cowboys from Hell	3	2016-03-23 02:20:09.766929	2016-03-25 22:16:14.004562	2019
6	Geckos 2016 Preseason Report	The two-time Franklin Fantasy Baseball League champions boast one of the richest farm systems in the game. Shortstop Orlando Arcia and first baseman A.J. Reed highlight a system that in 2016 includes nine Baseball America Top 100 prospects.\r\n\r\nReed, a slugging first baseman, could contribute to the Geckos as soon as 2016.\r\n\r\nLong known for their ability to develop top-flight starting pitchers, the Geckos bolstered their stable of arms with the additions of Jake Thompson, Michael Fulmer and Luis Ortiz in 2016. Those three look to join established big league arms Jake Odorizzi and Joe Ross in the Geckos' rotation of the future.\r\n\r\nIf this system has a weakness, it is up the middle. Only Arcia projects as an up-the-middle starter for the Geckos in 2016. The organization also must bolster its catching depth to compete in the future.	A.J. Reed, 1B	Orlando Arcia, SS	Ryan McMahon, 3B	Jake Thompson, RHP	Michael Fulmer, RHP	Luis Ortiz, RHP	Cornelius Randolph, OF	Daz Cameron, OF	Bobby Bradley, 1B	Brandon Drury, 3B	Brian McCann	Eric Hosmer	Starlin Castro	Jake Lamb	Orlando Arcia	Marcell Ozuna	Adam Eaton	David Peralta	A.J. Reed	Ryan McMahon	Clayton Kershaw	Jake Odorizzi	Jordan Zimmermann	Zach Britton	Michael Fulmer	Erasmo Ramirez	Joe Ross	Jake Thompson								2016	2015	2014	2013	2012	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	A.J. Reed, 1B	Steven Matz, LHP	Jake Odorizzi, RHP	Jonathan Singleton, 1B	Arodys Vizcaino, RHP						Geckos (AAA)	Scranton Yankees	Geckos	Shaolin Schmeckles	Young Tommy Toolsheds						2016	2015	2014	2013	2012	2011	2010	2009	2008	2007	Cornelius Randolph, OF	Kyle Freeland, LHP	Tommy Hunter, RP	Byron Buxton, OF	Jed Bradley, LHP	Josh Sale, OF	Jose Iglesias, SS	Christian Friedrich, LHP	Madison Bumgarner, LHP	Seth McClung, RHP	Geckos (AAA)	Free agent	Free agent	Supreme Clientele (AAA)	Free agent	Free agent	Free agent	Free agent	Cowboys From Hell	Free agent	2	2016-04-04 21:31:07.731136	2016-04-04 21:38:53.853409	2019
