2	4	8	This book was really neat. Or, in the words of the great Brian Risica, "rly gr8t." I liked reading about all of Tyson's bouts and all of his exploits in Brownsville and other places around the globe. Who knew he introduced cocaine to the Romanian Mafia!? That's crazy for sure. Anyway, my biggest disappointment in this entire book is Tyson's complete lack of giving a shit about his own video game. That game was sick and a staple in every kids home back in our day. He really didn't care at all about it. "like rly," -Brian Risica. I wish he played it more and would have enjoyed it as much as we did. But then again, he lived that life, he actually knocked out Glass Joe! Cray.	2015-11-20 14:59:42.067669	2015-11-20 14:59:42.067669
3	4	4	Just Fin McLeod getting into more and more shenanigans!	2015-12-01 20:03:34.911269	2015-12-01 20:03:34.911269
4	1	8	The lack of reviews here could make a guy feel like El Smucko!  \r\n\r\nAnyway, this book was filled with stories and situations that seem 100% unbelievable.  From the sheer quantity of cocaine carried and used, to implying a Cadillac Escalade isn't even nice enough to give to a prostitute... the entire thing seems fake and blown out of proportion; however, it IS Mike Tyson.  I don't think he has a eidetic memory,  I'm not sure these stories are accurate, and I know for certain many of his 'facts' aren't even remotely factual, but I believe that HE believes it all to be the truth.\r\n\r\nTHE GUY HIT AND GOT HIT FOR A LIVING!!  Of course his stories and memories are going to be out of wack, but I found it only added to my enjoyment of the book.  I don't care if the stories were blown out of proportion, it was very entertaining!\r\n\r\nOh, and remember all:  \r\n\r\n"It's not a lie, if you believe it."\r\n-G. Costanza	2015-12-07 17:17:48.316805	2015-12-07 17:17:48.316805
5	4	8	Matty B with some really great thoughts here. "you mean rly great" - Riz	2015-12-27 04:35:19.257967	2015-12-27 04:35:19.257967
6	4	2	I think my favorite character is the guy that reminds me of Brett Amidon.	2015-12-27 04:35:53.867657	2015-12-27 04:35:53.867657
7	4	9	Tom Kalinske loves him some Sake! We should all drink Sake to commemorate this great book. Also, bought an NES due to this book, making it the most expensive book for me so far. Great memories from some really rad games. RC PRO-AM!	2015-12-27 04:36:52.605315	2015-12-27 04:36:52.605315
8	2	9	"It's-a me, Mario!" A nice look back at the "Console Wars" of the late 1980s and early 1990s!	2015-12-31 21:17:42.245545	2015-12-31 21:17:42.245545
